# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# White-label identity protection (APP repo)
#
# This is the MASTER (meow-live) codebase. Client apps (jo, lumio, kitty, ...)
# live on their own branches and merge code/feature changes FROM this master.
# A client's brand IDENTITY must NEVER be overwritten by such a merge.
#
# The files listed below are 100% per-client and are kept as the CLIENT's
# version ("ours") on every merge from master, via a one-line merge driver that
# must be defined once per clone:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# tools/merge-from-master.sh configures that automatically and also re-applies
# the line-level identity that lives inside shared files (applicationId, app
# label, iOS display name) — those can't use this whole-file mechanism.
#
# NOTE: merge=ours only keeps the client's version of files that exist on BOTH
# sides. New asset files added on master still flow into the client normally
# (a new feature's new icon is delivered; the client's existing brand art is
# never clobbered). That is exactly the white-label behaviour we want.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shell tooling must stay LF (CRLF breaks bash on checkout)
*.sh text eol=lf

# Firebase project identity (Android google-services + iOS plist + FlutterFire)
android/app/google-services.json         merge=ours
ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist      merge=ours
firebase.json                            merge=ours

# Android launcher icon, splash & background
android/app/src/main/res/mipmap*/**      merge=ours
android/app/src/main/res/drawable*/**    merge=ours

# iOS app icon & launch images
ios/Runner/Assets.xcassets/**            merge=ours

# In-app brand assets (logo, badges, ui icons, ...)
assets/**/*.png    merge=ours
assets/**/*.jpg    merge=ours
assets/**/*.jpeg   merge=ours
assets/**/*.webp   merge=ours
assets/**/*.gif    merge=ours
assets/**/*.svg    merge=ours
